This is my second Ascension. First was with a Wizard.
I tried many characters, and would reach the gehennom with them, but
never had the time to complete them. This time I had a full week to
complete this game. The first time I somehow did not post my
ascension.

I have been playing ranger for a very long time, almost a year. But
never managed to complete one before I got sucked into work and then
lost interest in the character.

In this game Ran1 started as usual going down to Sokoban, relying on
pets and only gaining 2 levels while doing so. She had prayed on the
way with low hit points to gain some hit points after 300 moves. In
Sokoban she killed the mimics before they could kill the 2 large pet
dogs. She was level 5 when returning from Sokoban with the bag of
holding. She had found a stethoscope by this time making it easier to
manage pets.

This game had been low on useful articles. Ran1 did not find a key or
a pick-axe until quite late that is quite a bit below the minetown.
Also the mithril was missing. The only shop in the dungeon was
locked so without a key it was left alone. She did loot all the shops
except for Izchak's because of the pathetic returns on buying and
selling the few candles he had. She lost her tripes to a stupidity in
the first shop which cost a lot of turns.

There had been a lot of food, in the early game. And Rangers start
with a lot of food ;-).

On the way to the minesend Ran1 had a trouble with a cockatrice,
luckily the amulet he had found was life-saving. At the same point
just a little bit earlier she had been careless and had been reduced
to one hit point, and the pray saved her. She had no lizard corpse to
prevent the stiffening. This was the only near death scenario in the
whole game.

After this it was smooth sailing except for the lack of items. By the
time Ran1 reached medusa she had gained enough levels to be admitted
to the Quest. The Scorpius was easy to kill with expert blessed +2
orcish arrows, fired from orcish bow. She had found one enchant weapon
by that time, which had made it easier to use them. Also altars where
quite rare. Other than the minetown (which was converted because of
lack of holy water), there was one at level 18 (which was a temple)
and level 19. She made the 19 one as the base. She danced with the
Nurses after cursing the scroll of genocide and unholy water she had
found. This gave her around 100hitpoints.

Ran1 completed the castle by masterminding it but never managing to
kill monsters with the drawbridge. She could play the passtune, but
somehow couldn't see any monsters die. So she took the back path.
After getting the wand of wishing she came back to the base and had a
long long sac fest till she got crowned. She didn't take any
precautions except dropping the luckstone, before praying. She managed
to get about half a dozen spellbooks and a dozen golden glows and
about 7 points of AC. She had been AC:0 naked before this, making her
an easy 49AC at the end of the whole excercise.

Also during this whole thing she learnt many spells. She used the robe
from the minetown priest, an amulet of reflection from a death drop.
She had obtained the GDSM from an extra magic lamp that She had found.
She did not rub her first magic lamp. She found speed boots and helm
of
brilliance from polymorphing objects from the 7 charges of the wand.
Rest of the AK was normal stuff. She never found or polymorphed a
T-Shirt.

She wished for 4 magic markers to enchant all the armour, and
rustproof and enchant all the darts she had found, about 300. She
later obtained two magic markers via polymorphs, but never did find
any in the normal way. There are a few dart traps in the VotD. She had
polymorphed to obtain spellbook of Identify, magic mapping and Detect
treasures. For some reason the really useful things where always
missing. She obtained the rings of free action and conflict via
polymorph. She later found the two together in the Wizards tower. She
found no grease in the game only obtained it (5 charges) from a
polymorphed spent magic marker.

She found 3 wands of death total. One before Orcus and the other in
Air.

Ran1 summoned and then killed Yeeghnou during the sac-fest.  She found
an glass orb (the only one) which she blessed and used for the planes.
She had kept some backup cursed gold detection scrolls in case the orb
broke (which it didn't).

She had more than a 350hp, and 49AC before starting the Ascension run.

Vlad was his usual self, and Wizard only troubled her 4 times. Ran1
teleported down from Wizards castle to the lowest level then did the
invokation ritual which didn't seem to work properly, because she was
interrupted a lot. After this she teleported down to the sanctum. She
had found only one potion of gain level (not even while polymorphing),
although she had seen other monsters drink them sometimes. And this
was near the VS. But it was not cursed and she had not carried unholy
water. She had concentrated on running away after killing the priest.
She had once fainted in the Sanctum, but nobody was really following
her very closely, maybe due to speed maybe due to conflict. She had it
on the whole time in the Sanctum and the planes.

Ran1 did not take off the ring of free action ever during the run. She
was taking off her teleport control ring once in a while and the
jumpiness was causing some problem. After moving two levels up she
carelessly dropped through a hole back into Sanctum, but well it was
not that tough.

She was able to kill the Wizard all four times with the WoDeath,
before
it could cause some real problems. She had blessed everything useful
before leaving the base. And did not stop very long at the base on the
way back. Being a chaotic the mysterious force was not very bad, she
probably was thrown back only 4-5 times.

The planes were very easy the Ascension run was completed in about an
hour of realtime. In Astral she was placed on the right which was
guarded
by famine and it succumbed to death. She had to uncurse her Stormy
before she could put back her =3DoC before entering the doorway to
Famine.
The right also turned out to be the chaotic altar and there was much
rejoicing.



